    "id": "so-simba-cdr-of-antarctic-sea-ice-thickness-and-sea-ice-volume",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This climate data record of sea ice thickness and volume is obtained from individual radar altimeters (Envisat, CryoSat-2). The processing chain features: 1) Retracking and along-track processing based on SI-CCI+ using Pysiral processing chain https://github.com/pysiral/pysiral 2) conversion from radar freeboard to sea ice freeboard and sea ice thickness using AMSR-E, SSMIS and AMSR-2 based snow depth 3) correct the position of the ice parcels using the DriftAware-SIAlt module https://github.com/robertricker/DriftAware-SIAlt using CDR sea ice drift 4) Computation of sea ice volume and mass from the sea ice thickness. This dataset was generated by NORCE, Norwegian Research Centre and funded by ESA Polar Science Cluster project SO-SIMBA. The ESA CCI Program contributed with Research and Development on the algorithms.",
